# Create Terraform Module (GCP)

Scaffold a new `{{MODULE_PREFIX}}-{name}` directory following GCP workspace conventions.

## Usage
Provide the module name as the argument: `$ARGUMENTS`

If no name is given, ask for:
- Module name (lowercase, hyphenated)
- Primary GCP resource type(s) (e.g., `google_storage_bucket`, `google_cloud_run_v2_service`)
- Optional features: {{OPTIONAL_FEATURES}}

## Directory Structure

```
{{MODULE_PREFIX}}-{name}/
├── main.tf                    # Provider requirements + data sources
├── {resource}.tf              # Core resource(s)
├── locals.tf                  # Name construction, label merging
├── variables.tf               # Module-specific variables
├── {{COMMON_VARS_FILE}}       # Standard cross-module variables
├── outputs.tf                 # Module outputs
├── versions.tf                # Version constraints
├── README.md                  # Documentation
├── .pre-commit-config.yaml    # Validation hooks
├── .tflint.hcl                # TFLint rules
├── .terraform-docs.yml        # Doc generation
├── examples/
│   └── basic/
│       ├── main.tf
│       └── variables.tf
└── tests/
    └── {resource}.tftest.hcl  # Native terraform tests
```

## File Templates

### versions.tf
```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = ">=1.3"
  required_providers {
    {{PROVIDER_BLOCK}}
  }
}
```
<!-- GCP default: google = { source = "hashicorp/google", version = ">=5.0,<6.0" } -->

### locals.tf
```hcl
locals {
  {{NAMING_LOCALS}}
  {{TAG_MERGE_LOCAL}}
}
```
<!-- GCP uses `labels` instead of `tags`. Name: labels = merge(var.env_default_labels, var.labels) -->

### Resource file
```hcl
resource "{{PROVIDER_RESOURCE}}" "{{RESOURCE_IDENTIFIER}}" {
  name    = local.name
  project = var.project
  region  = var.region
  labels  = local.labels
}
```
<!-- Note: not all GCP resources accept `name`, `region`, or `labels` — check the provider docs.
     GCS buckets use `location` instead of `region`. Cloud SQL uses `region`.
     GCP does not have a resource_group equivalent — resources are scoped to project. -->

### outputs.tf
```hcl
output "name" {
  value       = {{PROVIDER_RESOURCE}}.{{RESOURCE_IDENTIFIER}}.name
  description = "Name of the resource."
}

output "id" {
  value       = {{PROVIDER_RESOURCE}}.{{RESOURCE_IDENTIFIER}}.id
  description = "The ID of the resource."
}
```

### Test file
```hcl
mock_provider "google" {}

{{DATA_SOURCE_OVERRIDE}}

variables {
{{TEST_STANDARD_VARIABLES}}
}

run "creates_resource_with_correct_name" {
  command = plan
  assert {
    condition     = {{PROVIDER_RESOURCE}}.{{RESOURCE_IDENTIFIER}}.name == "{{EXPECTED_NAME_PATTERN}}"
    error_message = "Name should follow naming convention"
  }
}

run "merges_labels_correctly" {
  command = plan
  variables {
    labels = { extra = "label" }
  }
  assert {
    condition     = {{PROVIDER_RESOURCE}}.{{RESOURCE_IDENTIFIER}}.labels["extra"] == "label"
    error_message = "Custom labels should be merged"
  }
}
```

## Post-Creation

Run these commands after scaffolding:
```bash
cd {{MODULE_PREFIX}}-{name}
terraform fmt -recursive
terraform validate
terraform test
```
